    "text": "Every modern weapon has a brain. A cruise missile has to know where it is, where it's going, and how to get there, hundreds of miles away, flying low to dodge radar. That brain is made of chips. In twenty twenty two, researchers at the British think tank RUSI took apart Russian weapons recovered in Ukraine, from cruise missiles to radios to drones. They found more than four hundred fifty foreign made components. Three hundred eighteen of them came from American companies. A single Kh one oh one cruise missile contained thirty one foreign parts.",
